1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,400
Can has no booking. He asks the shared printer to unlock. (simulated printer)

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,900
Refused: the printer checks its own NEAR account first. No booking, no print.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:14,500
A shared machine's money and rules usually sit in one admin's spreadsheet. Here they live in its own keyless NEAR account.

4
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:20,600
Booking is a NEAR transaction: a fee plus a refundable deposit. (simulated printer)

5
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,100
Ali's booking on testnet: reservation_confirmed.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,400
With a valid booking, the bridge unlocks the printer and the job starts. (simulated)

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:36,700
Telemetry crosses a rule, so the machine's agent opens an upkeep task. (demo threshold)

8
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:41,000
The agent's task on testnet, with its reason. Demo threshold 0.5 h (production 200 h).

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,300
Ayşe does the upkeep. Mehmet, another member, approves it.

10
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:49,300
She earns usage rights for this machine: non-transferable cards.

11
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:53,800
The machine keeps a small operating float, capped at 3 NEAR.

12
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:58,900
Everything above the cap is swept to the community's DAO treasury.

13
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:06,533
A council member tries to take Ayşe's right. Refused on chain: E_NON_TRANSFERABLE.

14
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:16,133
Check it yourself: ./scripts/verify.sh re-reads every claim from testnet, no keys needed.

15
00:01:16,033 --> 00:01:20,833
Same contract, different machines and rules: twelve profiles run in simulation.
